# Citation metadata, Citation File Format 1.2.0.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AI_GO: a single-file decision-tree engine, published with UNIL's questionnaire as reference content"
abstract: "A guided decision-tree engine for websites, delivered as one HTML file: six comment markers divide the file: the adopting institution's content sits between the second and the third, its heading and standfirst between the third and the fourth, and the engine between the fourth and the fifth. No build step, no dependency, no network request. The engine handles branching, history, session resumption, translation, screen-reader announcements and a fail-closed publication guard; a companion validator page runs the engine of the file it is given, so the publication verdict exists in one place only. It was written for the University of Lausanne questionnaire published as AI_GO. BSD-3-Clause covers the engine, the validator and the test harness; the example content block and the tree format are CC0-1.0; the questionnaire content in reference/ and docs/ARBRE.md is all rights reserved and is not licensed for reuse, see LICENSE."
# The people credited on the published tool. A harvested citation that named
# only the unit would drop the authors of the reasoning the tool carries.
